# livespec `work-supply` — host timer unit TEMPLATE, one instance per tenant.
#
# The factory's drain is an ENGINE somebody has to run. Measured 2026-10-13 on
# hp: the fleet Fabro server (cap 10) received no new run between about 18:27Z
# and 22:56Z while 0 runs were in flight, the Claude credential probe reported
# `usable`, and dispatch-ready work existed — because no session happened to be
# running `dispatcher.py loop`. Dispatch resumed only when some session started
# an engine again. Supply of work to the factory is therefore a clock question,
# exactly as run inventory is (see the `reconcile-runs` sibling), and not a
# question of who is logged in.
#
# The launcher path and the per-instance environment directory below are
# placeholder tokens that `install.sh` in this directory substitutes. Do NOT
# install this file verbatim.
#
# This is a systemd INSTANCE template: `%i` is the tenant instance name, and
# `install.sh` writes one `<instance>.env` per tenant into that environment
# directory, carrying that tenant's checkout path, drain budget, credential
# wrapper, and the OPERATOR IDENTITY AND HOME the pass runs under. A firing
# whose env file is incomplete therefore reads an EMPTY value and the launcher
# refuses, naming the variable, rather than draining some other repository or
# resolving some other account's plugin build.
#
# THREE THINGS THIS UNIT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO.
#
# It does not name a plugin build. `reconcile-runs` substitutes a plugin root
# at install time, which pins that unit to one cache build for ever: after a
# release the timer keeps executing the build the operator has already
# replaced, with no warning of its own — the stale-build trap AGENTS.md records
# against long-lived sessions, arriving through a unit file instead. The
# launcher resolves the tenant's REGISTERED install at each firing, and refuses
# rather than guessing when the tenant has none.
#
# It does not go through the credential wrapper. The wrapper is invoked once,
# by the detached pass itself. A wrapped launcher would make the pass's own
# wrapper call a NESTED one, and a nested call is what poisons the wrapper's
# 300-second credential cache for every other caller on the host (AGENTS.md,
# §"Beads runtime prerequisites"). The launcher needs no credential: it reads a
# JSON registry and starts a unit.
#
# It does not declare `User=`, and that omission is a DECISION rather than an
# oversight — identity and detachment are one question here, not two. The
# launcher's whole job is to hand the pass to a system-scope transient unit,
# and a non-root caller of `systemd-run --unit` needs polkit authorization it
# cannot obtain from a timer with no seat and no agent. So the FIRING runs as
# root and the PASS drops: the launcher passes the operator identity and home
# the instance environment file names (`--uid`, `--setenv HOME=`) to
# `systemd-run`, so the drain executes as the operator even though the firing
# that started it did not.
#
# The cost of that decision, paid here: systemd sets `$HOME` only for a unit
# declaring `User=` (systemd.exec(5)), so this unit's own environment carries
# NONE. Every `$HOME`-derived path a firing needs is therefore named in the
# instance environment file rather than inferred — the Claude Code plugin
# registry the launcher reads to resolve the build, and the `$HOME` the pass
# itself resolves `fabro` under. A launcher that fell back to an unset `$HOME`
# would compose `/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json`, refuse on every
# firing of every instance, and read as a tenant with no registered install;
# it refuses by NAMING the unresolvable variable instead.
#
# `Type=oneshot` is correct ONLY because ExecStart is the launcher rather than
# the drain. systemd never starts a oneshot that is still active, and a drain
# pass blocks until its wave's post-verdict stages finish — hours, for one
# wave. An ExecStart that ran the drain would therefore make the timer skip
# every firing for the length of the pass, which is the opposite of the
# guarantee this unit exists to provide.

[Unit]
Description=livespec work supply — one unattended drain pass for tenant %i
Documentation=https://github.com/thewoolleyman/livespec-orchestrator-beads-fabro
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
EnvironmentFile=@INSTANCE_ENV_DIR@/%i.env
ExecStart=@LAUNCHER@ --instance %i
# The launcher reads one JSON file and starts one transient unit; it never
# waits on the pass. A minute is generous and bounds a wedged registry read.
TimeoutStartSec=60
# A failed firing is not an incident: the next tick asks the same question
# again, and a restart storm against an unreadable registry would be noise.
Restart=no
